load ../agent-provider-binding.maude

--- Fixture discipline: every agent in a WHIPPLESCRIPT-AGENT-PROVIDER-BINDING
--- fixture carries exactly ONE boundTo. That is the premise under test, not an
--- accident of the fixtures -- the -ROUTED module is where it is dropped, and
--- the contrast between the two is the whole result.

--- Coverage: the sound design is not vacuous. An agent bound to the cleared
--- endpoint runs a secret turn, and the secret does reach that endpoint.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-AGENT-PROVIDER-BINDING :
  boundTo(a1, onprem) tell(a1, secret)
  =>* C:Cfg admitted(a1, secret) shipped(onprem, secret) .

--- Coverage: accumulation is real. After a secret turn, a LATER public turn to
--- the same agent still ships the earlier secret -- the append-only property
--- that makes routing unsound is present in this module too. It is safe here
--- only because the endpoint cannot change.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-AGENT-PROVIDER-BINDING :
  boundTo(a1, onprem) tell(a1, secret) tell(a1, public)
  =>* C:Cfg admitted(a1, public) shipped(onprem, secret) .

--- Coverage: the workflow pattern (section 3). Two agents at different tiers --
--- a1 cleared and holding the secret, a2 uncleared and running public turns --
--- both make progress. This is the composition unit the note prescribes.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-AGENT-PROVIDER-BINDING :
  boundTo(a1, onprem) boundTo(a2, cloud) tell(a1, secret) tell(a2, public)
  =>* C:Cfg admitted(a1, secret) admitted(a2, public) .

--- THE HEADLINE. Under a fixed per-agent binding, no label ever reaches an
--- endpoint not cleared for it -- across both agents, both endpoints, and any
--- interleaving of the four turns. The per-tell check is sound because the
--- binding cannot move. No solution.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-AGENT-PROVIDER-BINDING :
  boundTo(a1, onprem) boundTo(a2, cloud)
  tell(a1, secret) tell(a1, public) tell(a2, secret) tell(a2, public)
  =>* leak(P:Prov, L:Label) RESIDUAL:Cfg .

--- Bite: fail-closed at the tell. An agent bound to the uncleared endpoint
--- never runs a secret turn at all -- the secret never enters that
--- conversation's context in the first place. No solution.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-AGENT-PROVIDER-BINDING :
  boundTo(a2, cloud) tell(a2, secret)
  =>* admitted(a2, secret) RESIDUAL:Cfg .

--- Bite: context does not leak ACROSS agents. a1 holds the secret and a2 is
--- bound to the uncleared endpoint; a2's turns ship a2's transcript only. This
--- is what makes the two-agent workflow a real separation rather than a naming
--- convention. No solution.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-AGENT-PROVIDER-BINDING :
  boundTo(a1, onprem) boundTo(a2, cloud)
  tell(a1, secret) tell(a2, public)
  =>* shipped(cloud, secret) RESIDUAL:Cfg .

--- Coverage: THE NEGATIVE FIXTURE, and the reason the headline has content.
--- With per-turn routing the same four facts reach a leak: the secret turn goes
--- to onprem (correctly), the public turn routes to cloud (correctly, on its
--- own inputs), and the accumulated secret ships to cloud behind it.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-AGENT-PROVIDER-BINDING-ROUTED :
  available(onprem) available(cloud) tell(a1, secret) tell(a1, public)
  =>* C:Cfg leak(cloud, secret) .

--- Coverage: the precise witness, so the failure cannot be read as the routing
--- rule simply ignoring clearance. The public turn IS admitted and IS routed to
--- cloud on its own merits, while the conversation already holds the secret.
--- Every local decision is correct and the composition still discloses.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-AGENT-PROVIDER-BINDING-ROUTED :
  available(onprem) available(cloud) tell(a1, secret) tell(a1, public)
  =>* C:Cfg admitted(a1, public) routedTo(a1, cloud) ctx(a1, secret) leak(cloud, secret) .
